From: IoTGuard Stage 7 lab
Subject: [PATCH] soc: xlnx zynq7000: map SLCR when GEM is enabled

Upstream gap (Zephyr v4.4.2): drivers/ethernet/eth_xlnx_gem.c reads/writes
the GEM TX clock control register in SLCR (gem reg index 1, e.g. 0xf8000140
for gem0) during device init, but soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c only maps
gem reg index 0 (0xe000b000). On a bare boot (no u-boot PS7 init, e.g. QEMU
-kernel direct boot) the access raises a 1st level translation fault:

  eth_xlnx_gem_configure_clocks -> sys_read32(0xf8000140) -> DATA ABORT

Fix: map the SLCR node region whenever a GEM is enabled, so the driver can
program the clock dividers itself. This mirrors what the qemu_cortex_a9
board needs for QEMU user networking with cadence_gem.

Applied on the stage-7 Ubuntu workspace (~/zephyr-stage7/zephyr) for the
IoTGuard Zephyr-Sensor-01 firmware; kept as a file for reproducibility.
---
 soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c b/soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c
--- a/soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c
+++ b/soc/xlnx/zynq7000/common/soc.c
@@ -40,3 +40,15 @@ static const struct arm_mmu_region mmu_regions[] = {
+/* SLCR: eth_xlnx_gem programs GEM TX clock divisors in SLCR (gem reg idx 1)
+ * during init; without this mapping a bare boot (no PS7/u-boot init, e.g.
+ * QEMU -kernel) takes a translation fault on that access.
+ */
+#if DT_NODE_HAS_STATUS_OKAY(DT_NODELABEL(gem0)) || \
+	DT_NODE_HAS_STATUS_OKAY(DT_NODELABEL(gem1))
+	MMU_REGION_FLAT_ENTRY("slcr",
+			      DT_REG_ADDR(DT_NODELABEL(slcr)),
+			      DT_REG_SIZE(DT_NODELABEL(slcr)),
+			      MT_DEVICE | MATTR_SHARED | MPERM_R | MPERM_W),
+#endif
+
 /* GEMs */
 #if DT_NODE_HAS_STATUS_OKAY(DT_NODELABEL(gem0))
 	MMU_REGION_FLAT_ENTRY("gem0",
--
2.34.1
